{"trial_id": "sb__lake-warming-attribution__sz20__easy__s2", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "lake-warming-attribution", "pool_size": 20, "noise_mode": "easy", "seed": 2, "gt_slugs": ["contribution-analysis", "meteorology-driver-classification", "pca-decomposition", "trend-analysis"], "gt_positions": [4, 6, 7, 19], "n_candidates": 20, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 73.5, "agent_stdout_tail": "Both output files are written successfully:\n\n**`trend_result.csv`**\n- **Slope:** ~0.0805 \u00b0C/year \u2014 lake surface temperature is warming over time\n- **p-value:** ~0.0548 \u2014 marginally significant trend (just above the 0.05 threshold)\n\n**`dominant_factor.csv`**\n- **Dominant category:** **Heat** (AirTempLake, Shortwave radiation, Longwave radiation)\n- **Contribution:** **41%** of the variance in water warming\n\n**Summary of methodology:**\n1. **Trend analysis** \u2014 Linear regression (scipy `linregress`) on annual WaterTemperature vs. Year across 16 data points (2006\u20132021).\n2. **Contribution analysis** \u2014 Global PCA (4 components) on all 9 predictor variables standardized together, then R\u00b2 decomposition: each factor's contribution = Full R\u00b2 minus R\u00b2 when that factor is withheld. Factors were mapped to categories (Heat/Flow/Wind/Human) by their dominant loading variable, and contributions were summed per category.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "============================= test session starts ==============================\ncollecting ... collected 2 items\n\n.tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_trend_result FAILED [ 50%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_dominant_factor PASSED [100%]\n\n=================================== FAILURES ===================================\n_________________ TestLakeWarmingAttribution.test_trend_result _________________\n\nself = <test_outputs.TestLakeWarmingAttribution object at 0xe435505bade0>\n\n    def