{"trial_id": "sb__lake-warming-attribution__sz20__easy__s4", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "lake-warming-attribution", "pool_size": 20, "noise_mode": "easy", "seed": 4, "gt_slugs": ["contribution-analysis", "meteorology-driver-classification", "pca-decomposition", "trend-analysis"], "gt_positions": [2, 3, 7, 11], "n_candidates": 20, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 81.1, "agent_stdout_tail": "Both analyses are complete. Here's a summary:\n\n**Trend Analysis (`trend_result.csv`)**\n- **Slope**: 0.09 \u00b0C/year\n- **p-value**: 0.03 (significant at \u03b1=0.05)\n- The lake surface temperature shows a **statistically significant long-term warming trend**.\n\n**Dominant Driving Factor (`dominant_factor.csv`)**\n- **Category**: **Heat** (Air Temperature, Shortwave & Longwave radiation)\n- **Contribution**: **54%** of the variance in water temperature\n- Heat-related variables dominate over Flow (4%), Human (6%), and Wind factors, making it by far the most important driver of lake warming.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": true, "test_log_tail": "============================= test session starts ==============================\ncollecting ... collected 2 items\n\n.tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_trend_result PASSED [ 50%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_dominant_factor PASSED [100%]\n\n==================================== PASSES ====================================\n=========================== short test summary info ============================\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_trend_result\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_dominant_factor\n============================== 2 passed in 0.00s ===============================\n\n--- stderr ---\n", "system_prompt_chars": 20879}
{"trial_id": "sb__lake-warming-attribution__sz20__easy__s3", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "lake-warming-attribution", "pool_size": 20, "noise_mode": "easy", "seed": 3, "gt_slugs": ["contribution-analysis", "meteorology-driver-classification", "pca-decomposition", "trend-analysis"], "gt_positions": [0, 2, 13, 17], "n_candidates": 20, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 95.3, "agent_stdout_tail": "Done. Both output files are saved:\n\n**`trend_result.csv`**\n| slope | p-value |\n|-------|---------|\n| 0.09  | 0.03    |\n\nThe Mann-Kendall test confirms a statistically significant **increasing trend** in lake surface water temperature (Sen's slope = +0.09 \u00b0C/year, p = 0.03).\n\n**`dominant_factor.csv`**\n| variable | contribution |\n|----------|-------------|\n| Heat     | 51          |\n\nUsing global PCA (varimax rotation) + R\u00b2 decomposition across all four driver categories (Heat, Flow, Wind, Human), **Heat** is the dominant driver, explaining **~51%** of the variance in water warming. The factor loaded most strongly on NetRadiation and AirTempLake, reflecting the thermal forcing from the atmosphere as the primary cause.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": true, "test_log_tail": "============================= test session starts ==============================\ncollecting ... collected 2 items\n\n.tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_trend_result PASSED [ 50%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_dominant_factor PASSED [100%]\n\n==================================== PASSES ====================================\n=========================== short test summary info ============================\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_trend_result\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_dominant_factor\n============================== 2 passed in 0.00s ===============================\n\n--- stderr ---\n", "system_prompt_chars": 20879}
{"trial_id": "sb__lake-warming-attribution__sz50__random__s0", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "lake-warming-attribution", "pool_size": 50, "noise_mode": "random", "seed": 0, "gt_slugs": ["contribution-analysis", "meteorology-driver-classification", "pca-decomposition", "trend-analysis"], "gt_positions": [9, 26, 36, 49], "n_candidates": 50, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 117.9, "agent_stdout_tail": "Both output files are ready. Here's a summary of the results:\n\n---\n\n### Part 1 \u2014 Trend Analysis (`trend_result.csv`)\n\n| slope | p-value |\n|-------|---------|\n| 0.0879 \u00b0C/year | 0.0343 |\n\nThe Mann-Kendall test confirms a **statistically significant long-term warming trend** (p < 0.05). Lake surface temperature is rising at ~0.088 \u00b0C per year.\n\n---\n\n### Part 2 \u2014 Dominant Driving Factor (`dominant_factor.csv`)\n\n| variable | contribution |\n|----------|-------------|\n| **Heat** | **55%** |\n\nUsing per-category PCA (PC1 per category) followed by R\u00b2 decomposition:\n- **Heat** (AirTempLake, Shortwave, Longwave): **55%** \u2190 dominant\n- **Human** (DevelopedArea, AgricultureArea): 34%\n- **Flow** (Precip, Inflow, Outflow): 11%\n- **Wind** (WindSpeedLake): ~0%\n\nThe **Heat** category is the most important driver, accounting for 55% of the explained variance in water warming \u2014 physically intuitive, as rising air temperatures and radiative forcing are the primary mechanisms heating lake surface water.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": true, "test_log_tail": "============================= test session starts ==============================\ncollecting ... collected 2 items\n\n.tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_trend_result PASSED [ 50%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_dominant_factor PASSED [100%]\n\n==================================== PASSES ====================================\n=========================== short test summary info ==========================