{"trial_id": "sb__lake-warming-attribution__sz50__hard__s2", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "lake-warming-attribution", "pool_size": 50, "noise_mode": "hard", "seed": 2, "gt_slugs": ["contribution-analysis", "meteorology-driver-classification", "pca-decomposition", "trend-analysis"], "gt_positions": [4, 24, 42, 49], "n_candidates": 50, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 97.0, "agent_stdout_tail": "Both output files are saved. Here's a summary:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Trend Analysis \u2192 `trend_result.csv`\n\n| slope | p-value |\n|-------|---------|\n| 0.0879 \u00b0C/year | 0.0343 |\n\nUsing the **Mann-Kendall test with Sen's slope**, the lake surface temperature shows a **statistically significant warming trend** (p = 0.034 < 0.05) of approximately **+0.088 \u00b0C per year** over the study period (2006\u20132022).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Dominant Driving Factor \u2192 `dominant_factor.csv`\n\n| variable | contribution |\n|----------|-------------|\n| Heat | 74% |\n\nUsing **PCA with varimax rotation + R\u00b2 decomposition**, the four driver categories were cleanly separated:\n\n| Category | Variables | Contribution |\n|----------|-----------|-------------|\n| **Heat** | AirTempLake, NetRadiation | **74%** |\n| Human | DevelopedArea, AgricultureArea | 25% |\n| Wind | WindSpeedLake | <1% |\n| Flow | Precip, Inflow, Outflow | <1% |\n\n**Heat** (air temperature + net radiation) is by far the dominant driver of lake warming, explaining ~74% of the variance.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "============================= test session starts ==============================\ncollecting ... collected 2 items\n\n.tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_trend_result PASSED [ 50%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_dominant_factor FAILED [100%]\n\n=================================== FAILURES ===================================\n_______________ TestLakeWarmingAttribution.test_dominant_factor _________