{"trial_id": "sb__lake-warming-attribution__sz50__easy__s3", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "lake-warming-attribution", "pool_size": 50, "noise_mode": "easy", "seed": 3, "gt_slugs": ["contribution-analysis", "meteorology-driver-classification", "pca-decomposition", "trend-analysis"], "gt_positions": [16, 26, 41, 44], "n_candidates": 50, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 78.1, "agent_stdout_tail": "Both output files are written successfully:\n\n**`trend_result.csv`**\n| slope | p-value |\n|-------|---------|\n| 0.0879 | 0.0343 |\n\nThe Mann-Kendall test confirms a statistically significant **increasing trend** (p = 0.034 < 0.05), with water temperature rising at ~0.088 \u00b0C/year over 2006\u20132022.\n\n---\n\n**`dominant_factor.csv`**\n| variable | contribution |\n|----------|-------------|\n| Heat | 41 |\n\nUsing PCA (4 components) + R\u00b2 decomposition:\n- **Heat** (AirTempLake, Shortwave, Longwave) \u2014 **41%**\n- Flow (Precip, Inflow, Outflow) \u2014 27%\n- Wind (WindSpeedLake) \u2014 3%\n- Human (DevelopedArea, AgricultureArea) \u2014 absorbed into Heat PC\n\n**Heat is the dominant driver**, contributing ~41% to the explained variance in lake warming, consistent with the physical expectation that thermal/radiation forcing drives surface water temperature.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": true, "test_log_tail": "============================= test session starts ==============================\ncollecting ... collected 2 items\n\n.tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_trend_result PASSED [ 50%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_dominant_factor PASSED [100%]\n\n==================================== PASSES ====================================\n=========================== short test summary info ============================\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_trend_result\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestLakeWarmingAttribution::test_dominant_factor\n============