{"trial_id": "sb__sales-pivot-analysis__sz5__easy__s2", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "sales-pivot-analysis", "pool_size": 5, "noise_mode": "easy", "seed": 2, "gt_slugs": ["pdf", "xlsx"], "gt_positions": [0, 3], "n_candidates": 5, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 309.3, "agent_stdout_tail": "`/root/demographic_analysis.xlsx` has been created with all 5 sheets and 4 pivot tables. Here's a summary of what was built:\n\n**Data pipeline:**\n- Extracted 2,454 SA2 regions from the 74-page `population.pdf`\n- Joined with `income.xlsx` on `SA2_CODE` \u2192 2,450 matched rows\n- Computed **Quarter** (Q1\u2013Q4) from global MEDIAN_INCOME quartile cuts: \u2264$51,436 / \u2264$58,213 / \u2264$65,778 / >$65,778\n- Computed **Total** = EARNERS \u00d7 MEDIAN_INCOME\n\n**Five sheets:**\n| # | Sheet | Type | Detail |\n|---|-------|------|--------|\n| 1 | Population by State | Pivot | Rows: STATE \u00b7 Values: Sum of POPULATION_2023 |\n| 2 | Earners by State | Pivot | Rows: STATE \u00b7 Values: Sum of EARNERS |\n| 3 | Regions by State | Pivot | Rows: STATE \u00b7 Values: Count of SA2 regions |\n| 4 | State Income Quartile | Pivot | Rows: STATE \u00b7 Cols: Quarter (Q1\u2013Q4) \u00b7 Values: Sum of EARNERS |\n| 5 | SourceData | Table | 2,450 rows with all original + derived columns |\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": true, "test_log_tail": "::TestPivotTableConfiguration::test_pivot_uses_correct_aggregation[State Income Quartile-sum-quarter]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestPivotTableConfiguration::test_pivot_col_field[State Income Quartile-sum-quarter]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSourceDataSheet::test_source_data_has_required_column[SA2_CODE-<lambda>]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSourceDataSheet::test_source_data_has_required_column[SA2_NAME-<lambda>]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSourceDataSheet::test_source_data_has_required_column[STATE-<lambda>]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSourceDataSheet::test_source_data_has_require