{"trial_id": "sb__video-filler-word-remover__sz50__easy__s4", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "video-filler-word-remover", "pool_size": 50, "noise_mode": "easy", "seed": 4, "gt_slugs": ["ffmpeg-video-editing", "filler-word-processing", "whisper-transcription"], "gt_positions": [12, 15, 17], "n_candidates": 50, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 235.3, "agent_stdout_tail": "Done. Here's a summary of what was produced:\n\n**`/root/annotations.json`** \u2014 130 filler word occurrences detected across the 4m 30s interview, with timestamps. Sample:\n```json\n[\n  {\"word\": \"so\",       \"timestamp\": 1.08},\n  {\"word\": \"you know\", \"timestamp\": 13.98},\n  {\"word\": \"like\",     \"timestamp\": 14.8},\n  ...\n]\n```\n\n**`/root/output.mp4`** \u2014 All 130 filler clips stitched together (~50 seconds, 640\u00d7360 h264/aac).\n\n**Pipeline used:**\n1. **Whisper `tiny` model** transcribed the video with word-level timestamps\n2. Single-word fillers (`um`, `uh`, `like`, `yeah`, `so`, `well`, `okay`, `basically`, `hmm`, `hum`, `mhm`) and two-word phrases (`you know`, `i mean`, `kind of`, `i guess`) were matched against the transcript\n3. Each filler clip was extracted with word-specific durations (e.g. 0.3s for `uh`, 0.55s for `you know`) via ffmpeg, then all clips were concatenated into the output video\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "  # written in by the subprocess implementations\n                # like _posixsubprocess\n                err_msg = err_msg.decode()\n            except ValueError:\n                exception_name = b'SubprocessError'\n                hex_errno = b'0'\n                err_msg = 'Bad exception data from child: {!r}'.format(\n                              bytes(errpipe_data))\n            child_exception_type = getattr(\n                    builtins, exception_name.decode('ascii'),\n                    SubprocessError)\n            if issubclass(child_exception_type, OSError) and hex_errno:\n                errno_num = int(hex_errno, 16)\n                if err_msg == \"noexec:chdir\":\n                    err_msg = \"\"\n                    # The error must be from chdir(cwd).\n                    err_filename = cwd\n                elif err_msg == \"noexec\":\n                    err_msg = \"\"\n                    err_filename = None\n                else:\n                    err_filename = orig_executable\n                if errno_num != 0:\n                    err_msg = os.strerror(errno_num)\n                if err_filename is not None:\n>                   raise child_exception_type(errno_num, err_msg, err_filename)\nE                   FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'ffprobe'\n\n/usr/local/lib/python3.12/subprocess.py:1955: FileNotFoundError\n==================================== PASSES ====================================\n=========================== short test summary info ============================\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestOutputs::test_annotations_file_exists\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestOutputs::test_annotations_format\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestOutputs::test_annotations_match_ground_truth\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestOutputs::test_z_copy_outputs_to_trajectory\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestOutputs::test_output_video_duration - File...\n========================= 1 failed, 4 passed in 0.04s ==========================\n\n--- stderr ---\n", "system_prompt_chars": 38919}
