{"trial_id": "sb__weighted-gdp-calc__sz10__hard__s3", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "weighted-gdp-calc", "pool_size": 10, "noise_mode": "hard", "seed": 3, "gt_slugs": ["xlsx"], "gt_positions": [3], "n_candidates": 10, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 364.4, "agent_stdout_tail": "All formulas are correctly written into `gdp.xlsx`. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n**Step 1 \u2014 Data lookup (H12:L17, H19:L24, H26:L31):**\nUsed `INDEX/MATCH` with two conditions \u2014 series code from column D and year from row 9:\n```\n=INDEX(Data!$B$21:$M$40, MATCH($D12, Data!$B$21:$B$40, 0), MATCH(H$9, Data!$B$4:$M$4, 0))\n```\nThis pulls exports, imports, and GDP for all 6 GCC countries across 2019\u20132023 from the Data sheet rows 21\u201340.\n\n**Step 2 \u2014 Net exports as % of GDP (H35:L40):**\n```\n=(H12-H19)/H26   \u2192 UAE\n=(H13-H20)/H27   \u2192 Bahrain\n... etc.\n```\nThen statistics for each year (min, max, median, simple mean, 25th, 75th percentiles) across all 6 countries.\n\n**Step 3 \u2014 GDP-weighted mean (H50:L50):**\n```\n=SUMPRODUCT(H35:H40, H26:H31) / SUM(H26:H31)\n```\nSpot-check for 2019: weighted mean NX/GDP \u2248 **12.2%** (Saudi Arabia's large GDP at a lower 8.0% NX/GDP ratio pulls the weighted mean below the simple average).\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_exports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_imports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_gdp_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_statistics_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_has_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoExcelErrors::test_no_formula_errors\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_no_extra_sheets_added\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_required_sheets_exist\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_task_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_data_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoMacros::test_no_vba_macros\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoMacros::test_file_extension_xlsx\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_exports_values - Ass...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_imports_values - Ass...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_gdp_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_values\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_min_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_max_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_median_values - Asse...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_mean_values - Assert...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_percentile_values - ...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_values_reasonable\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_values\n======================== 11 failed, 16 passed in 3.71s =========================\n\n--- stderr ---\n", "system_prompt_chars": 26798}
{"trial_id": "sb__sales-pivot-analysis__sz100__hard__s1", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "sales-pivot-analysis", "pool_size": 100, "noise_mode": "hard", "seed": 1, "gt_slugs": ["pdf", "xlsx"], "gt_positions": [85, 94], "n_candidates": 100, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 230.3, "agent_stdout_tail": "`/root/demographic_analysis.xlsx` has been created successfully. Here's a summary of what was built:\n\n---\n\n### Data pipeline\n- **Population PDF** (74 pages) \u2192 extracted 2,454 SA2 regions with `SA2_CODE`, `SA2_NAME`, `STATE`, `POPULATION_2023`\n- **Income XLSX** \u2192 2,450 rows with `SA2_CODE`, `EARNERS`, `MEDIAN_INCOME`, `MEAN_INCOME`\n- Inner-joined on `SA2_CODE` \u2192 **2,450 merged rows**\n\n### Quartile boundaries (based on `MEDIAN_INCOME` percentiles across all regions)\n| Quartile | MEDIAN_INCOME range |\n|----------|---------------------|\n| Q1 | \u2264 $51,436 |\n| Q2 | $51,437 \u2013 $58,213 |\n| Q3 | $58,214 \u2013 $65,778 |\n| Q4 | > $65,778 |\n\nEach quartile contains ~601\u2013602 regions (evenly distributed).\n\n### Workbook structure (5 sheets)\n| Sheet | Content |\n|-------|---------|\n| **Population by State** | Pivot \u2014 Rows: STATE \u2192 Sum of POPULATION_2023 |\n| **Earners by State** | Pivot \u2014 Rows: STATE \u2192 Sum of EARNERS |\n| **Regions by State** | Pivot \u2014 Rows: STATE \u2192 Count of SA2 regions |\n| **State Income Quartile** | Pivot \u2014 Rows: STATE \u00d7 Columns: Q1/Q2/Q3/Q4 \u2192 Sum of EARNERS |\n| **SourceData** | All 2,450 rows with original columns + `Quarter` + `Total` (EARNERS \u00d7 MEDIAN_INCOME) |\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": true, "test_log_tail": "::TestPivotTableConfiguration::test_pivot_uses_correct_aggregation[State Income Quartile-sum-quarter]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestPivotTableConfiguration::test_pivot_col_field[State Income Quartile-sum-quarter]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSourceDataSheet::test_source_data_has_required_column[SA2_CODE-<lambda>]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSourceDataSheet::test_source_data_has_required_column[SA2_NAME-<lambda>]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSourceDataSheet::test_source_data_has_required_column[STATE-<lambda>]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSourceDataSheet::test_source_data_has_required_column[POPULATION_2023-<lambda>]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSourceDataSheet::test_source_data_has_required_column[EARNERS-<lambda>]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSourceDataSheet::test_source_data_has_required_column[MEDIAN_INCOME-<lambda>]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSourceDataSheet::test_source_data_has_required_column[Quarter-<lambda>]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSourceDataSheet::test_source_data_has_required_column[Total-<lambda>]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSourceDataContent::test_source_data_has_reasonable_row_count\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSourceDataContent::test_quarter_values_are_valid\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSourceDataContent::test_state_values_are_valid\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestDataTransformationCorrectness::test_pivot_cache_has_fields\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestDataTransformationCorrectness::test_total_equals_earners_times_median_income\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestDataTransformationCorrectness::test_sa2_codes_from_income_file_present\nSKIPPED [1] .tests/test_outputs.py:81: 'Population by State' is not a matrix pivot\nSKIPPED [1] .tests/test_outputs.py:81: 'Earners by State' is not a matrix pivot\nSKIPPED [1] .tests/test_outputs.py:81: 'Regions by State' is not a matrix pivot\n======================== 23 passed, 3 skipped in 0.24s =========================\n\n--- stderr ---\n", "system_prompt_chars": 347309}
