{"trial_id": "sb__sales-pivot-analysis__sz100__hard__s3", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "sales-pivot-analysis", "pool_size": 100, "noise_mode": "hard", "seed": 3, "gt_slugs": ["pdf", "xlsx"], "gt_positions": [44, 48], "n_candidates": 100, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 362.8, "agent_stdout_tail": "The file has been created successfully at `/root/demographic_analysis.xlsx` (170KB). Here's a summary of what was built:\n\n---\n\n### `/root/demographic_analysis.xlsx` \u2014 5 sheets, 4 pivot tables\n\n**Data pipeline:**\n- **Population PDF** \u2192 2,454 SA2 regions across 9 Australian states/territories\n- **Income XLSX** \u2192 2,450 rows with EARNERS, MEDIAN_INCOME, MEAN_INCOME (45 rows had `np` = not provided)\n- Merged on `SA2_CODE` \u2192 2,454 rows in SourceData\n\n**Sheets created:**\n\n| # | Sheet | Type | Details |\n|---|-------|------|---------|\n| 1 | **Population by State** | Pivot table | Rows: STATE \u2192 Sum of POPULATION_2023 |\n| 2 | **Earners by State** | Pivot table | Rows: STATE \u2192 Sum of EARNERS |\n| 3 | **Regions by State** | Pivot table | Rows: STATE \u2192 Count of SA2 regions |\n| 4 | **State Income Quartile** | Pivot table (2D) | Rows: STATE, Cols: Q1/Q2/Q3/Q4, Values: Sum of EARNERS |\n| 5 | **SourceData** | Data table | All 2,454 rows \u00d7 9 columns |\n\n**SourceData enrichment:**\n- **Quarter** \u2014 based on `MEDIAN_INCOME` quartile boundaries across all regions (Q1 \u2264 $51,436 \u2264 Q2 \u2264 $58,213 \u2264 Q3 \u2264 $65,778 < Q4), yielding ~601 regions per quartile\n- **Total** \u2014 `EARNERS \u00d7 MEDIAN_INCOME` (blank where income data unavailable)\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "::TestPivotTableConfiguration::test_pivot_uses_correct_aggregation[State Income Quartile-sum-quarter]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestPivotTableConfiguration::test_pivot_col_field[State Income Quartile-sum-quarter]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSourceDataSheet::test_source_data_h