{"trial_id": "sb__weighted-gdp-calc__sz20__hard__s3", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "weighted-gdp-calc", "pool_size": 20, "noise_mode": "hard", "seed": 3, "gt_slugs": ["xlsx"], "gt_positions": [9], "n_candidates": 20, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 201.4, "agent_stdout_tail": "All 155 yellow cells filled, zero empty. `gdp.xlsx` is complete with:\n\n**Step 1 \u2014 `H12:L17`, `H19:L24`, `H26:L31`**  \nEach cell uses `=INDEX(Data!$H$21:$M$40, MATCH($D<row>, Data!$B$21:$B$40, 0), MATCH(<col>$9, Data!$H$4:$M$4, 0))` \u2014 a two-condition INDEX/MATCH lookup using the series code from column D and the year from row 9 in the Task sheet.\n\n**Step 2a \u2014 `H35:L40` (Net Exports % GDP)**  \n`=(H12-H19)/H26*100` pattern \u2014 exports minus imports divided by GDP times 100, for each country and year.\n\n**Step 2b \u2014 Statistics (rows 42\u201347)**  \nMIN, MAX, MEDIAN, AVERAGE, PERCENTILE(0.25), PERCENTILE(0.75) over the six countries for each year.\n\n**Step 3 \u2014 Weighted Mean (`H50:L50`)**  \n`=SUMPRODUCT(H26:H31, H35:H40)/SUM(H26:H31)` \u2014 GDP-weighted average of net exports % GDP. For 2019 this yields ~12.22% (vs. simple mean of ~13.07%), reflecting Saudi Arabia's large GDP weight pulling the average toward its lower net-export ratio.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_exports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_imports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_gdp_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_statistics_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_has_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoExcelErrors::test_no_formula_errors\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_no_extra_sheets_added\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::T