{"trial_id": "sb__offer-letter-generator__sz50__random__s3", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "offer-letter-generator", "pool_size": 50, "noise_mode": "random", "seed": 3, "gt_slugs": ["docx"], "gt_positions": [44], "n_candidates": 50, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 268.2, "agent_stdout_tail": "The offer letter has been filled successfully. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n- **Template**: Loaded `offer_letter_template.docx` with split-run placeholders (e.g., `{{COMP` + `ANY_NAME}}` across multiple XML runs)\n- **Replacement strategy**: Used paragraph-level text assembly \u2014 collected the full paragraph text, substituted all `{{KEY}}` values, then wrote back to the first run (clearing subsequent runs), which handles Word's split-placeholder behavior\n- **Conditional section**: Since `RELOCATION_PACKAGE` is `\"Yes\"`, kept the relocation content and stripped the `{{IF_RELOCATION}}` / `{{END_IF_RELOCATION}}` markers\n- **Nested tables**: Recursively processed nested tables containing Position, Department, Base Salary ($185,000), Signing Bonus ($25,000), Equity Shares (5,000), Start Date, Manager Name\n- **Verification**: No `{{...}}` placeholders remain; all 20 data fields including Sarah Chen's details are present\n\nThe filled document was saved to `/root/offer_letter_filled.docx` (via all sandbox work directories).\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": true, "test_log_tail": "test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[DEPARTMENT] PASSED       [ 72%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[BASE_SALARY] PASSED      [ 77%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[SIGNING_BONUS] PASSED    [ 83%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[EQUITY_SHARES] PASSED    [ 88%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[MANAGER_NAME] PASSED     [ 94%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_conditional_section PASSED                  [100%]\n\n==================================== PASSES ====================================\n======