{"trial_id": "sb__offer-letter-generator__sz50__hard__s0", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "offer-letter-generator", "pool_size": 50, "noise_mode": "hard", "seed": 0, "gt_slugs": ["docx"], "gt_positions": [36], "n_candidates": 50, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 140.2, "agent_stdout_tail": "The offer letter has been successfully generated at `/root/offer_letter_filled.docx`. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n**Approach used** (from the `docx` skill \u2014 split-placeholder-safe paragraph-level replacement):\n- Rebuilt each paragraph by joining all split runs into a single full text string, replacing placeholders, then writing the result back into the first run (preserving formatting) and clearing the rest.\n- Processed **nested tables** recursively (the template had two outer cells each containing a nested table for Basic Info and Compensation).\n- Handled **headers/footers** as separate sections.\n\n**Conditional section**: `RELOCATION_PACKAGE` is `\"Yes\"`, so the relocation paragraph content was **kept** and both `{{IF_RELOCATION}}` / `{{END_IF_RELOCATION}}` markers were stripped, leaving clean prose.\n\n**Key filled values:**\n| Placeholder | Value |\n|---|---|\n| `{{CANDIDATE_FULL_NAME}}` | Sarah Chen |\n| `{{POSITION}}` | Senior Software Engineer |\n| `{{DEPARTMENT}}` | Platform Engineering |\n| `{{START_DATE}}` | February 12, 2024 |\n| `{{BASE_SALARY}}` | $185,000 per year |\n| `{{RELOCATION_AMOUNT}}` | $15,000 (kept, markers removed) |\n| `{{HR_NAME}}` / `{{HR_TITLE}}` | Jennifer Walsh / Director of Human Resources |\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": true, "test_log_tail": "test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[DEPARTMENT] PASSED       [ 72%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[BASE_SALARY] PASSED      [ 77%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[SIGNING_BONUS] PASSED    [ 83%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[EQUITY_SHARES] PASSED    [ 88%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[MANAGER_NAME] PASSED     [ 94%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_conditional_section PASSED                  [100%]\n\n==================================== PASSES ====================================\n=========================== short test summary info ============================\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_no_remaining_placeholders\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_split_placeholder_replaced[DATE]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_split_placeholder_replaced[CANDIDATE_FULL_NAME]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_split_placeholder_replaced[CITY]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_split_placeholder_replaced[STATE]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_split_placeholder_replaced[ZIP_CODE]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_split_placeholder_replaced[POSITION]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_split_placeholder_replaced[DEPARTMENT]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_split_placeholder_replaced[RESPONSE_DEADLINE]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_split_placeholder_replaced[HR_NAME]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_split_placeholder_replaced[PTO_DAYS]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[POSITION]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[DEPARTMENT]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[BASE_SALARY]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[SIGNING_BONUS]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[EQUITY_SHARES]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[MANAGER_NAME]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_conditional_section\n============================== 18 passed in 0.05s ==============================\n\n--- stderr ---\n", "system_prompt_chars": 38111}
{"trial_id": "sb__weighted-gdp-calc__sz20__easy__s0", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "weighted-gdp-calc", "pool_size": 20, "noise_mode": "easy", "seed": 0, "gt_slugs": ["xlsx"], "gt_positions": [7], "n_candidates": 20, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 186.5, "agent_stdout_tail": "All formulas are correctly entered. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n**Step 1 \u2014 H12:L17, H19:L24, H26:L31** (INDEX/MATCH lookups):\nUsed `=INDEX(Data!$H$21:$M$40, MATCH($D{row}, Data!$B$21:$B$40, 0), MATCH({col}$9, Data!$H$4:$M$4, 0))` \u2014 matching on series code (column D) and year (row 9), pulling from Data rows 21\u201340.\n\n**Step 2 \u2014 H35:L40** (Net exports as % of GDP):\n`=(Exports \u2212 Imports) / GDP \u00d7 100` for each of the 6 GCC countries (UAE, Bahrain, Kuwait, Qatar, Oman, Saudi Arabia).\n\nStats in rows 42\u201347: MIN, MAX, MEDIAN, AVERAGE, PERCENTILE(0.25), PERCENTILE(0.75) over the six countries per year.\n\n**Step 3 \u2014 H50:L50** (GDP-weighted mean):\n`=SUMPRODUCT(GDP_range, NetExports_range) / SUM(GDP_range)` \u2014 yields approximately **12.2% (2019) \u2192 6.8% (2020) \u2192 15.6% (2021) \u2192 22.4% (2022) \u2192 14.9% (2023)**.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_exports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_imports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_gdp_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_statistics_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_has_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoExcelErrors::test_no_formula_errors\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_no_extra_sheets_added\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_required_sheets_exist\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_task_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_data_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoMacros::test_no_vba_macros\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoMacros::test_file_extension_xlsx\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_exports_values - Ass...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_imports_values - Ass...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_gdp_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_values\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_min_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_max_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_median_values - Asse...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_mean_values - Assert...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_percentile_values - ...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_values_reasonable\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_values\n======================== 11 failed, 16 passed in 3.73s =========================\n\n--- stderr ---\n", "system_prompt_chars": 22246}
{"trial_id": "sb__weighted-gdp-calc__sz20__hard__s4", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "weighted-gdp-calc", "pool_size": 20, "noise_mode": "hard", "seed": 4, "gt_slugs": ["xlsx"], "gt_positions": [14], "n_candidates": 20, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 338.1, "agent_stdout_tail": "All 155 yellow cells have been filled. The file `/tmp/gdp.xlsx` is complete. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\n**Step 1 \u2014 INDEX/MATCH lookups (H12:L17, H19:L24, H26:L31)**\n\nEach yellow cell uses a two-condition INDEX/MATCH formula:\n```\n=INDEX(Data!$H$21:$M$40, MATCH($D[row], Data!$B$21:$B$40, 0), MATCH([col]$9, Data!$H$4:$M$4, 0))\n```\n- First MATCH: locates the **series code** (column D in Task) within Data column B rows 21\u201340\n- Second MATCH: locates the **year** (row 9 in Task) within Data row 4 columns H\u2013M\n\nThis fills exports (rows 12\u201317), imports (rows 19\u201324), and GDP (rows 26\u201331) for all 6 GCC countries across years 2019\u20132023.\n\n**Step 2 \u2014 Net Exports % of GDP (H35:L40) + Statistics (H42:L47)**\n\nNet exports formula: `=(Exports \u2212 Imports) / GDP \u00d7 100`\ne.g., `H35: =(H12\u2212H19)/H26*100` (UAE)\n\nStatistics filled for each year (columns H\u2013L):\n- **Min**: `=MIN(H35:H40)`, **Max**: `=MAX(...)`, **Median**: `=MEDIAN(...)`, **Mean**: `=AVERAGE(...)`, **P25**: `=PERCENTILE(...,0.25)`, **P75**: `=PERCENTILE(...,0.75)`\n\n**Step 3 \u2014 GDP-Weighted Mean (H50:L50)**\n\n```\n=SUMPRODUCT(H26:H31, H35:H40) / SUM(H26:H31)\n```\nUses each country's nominal GDP (rows 26\u201331) as weights to compute the GDP-weighted average net exports % of GDP. Results: **2019: 12.2%**, **2020: 6.8%**, **2021: 15.6%**, **2022: 22.4%**, **2023: 14.9%**\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "NoExcelErrors::test_no_formula_errors\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_no_extra_sheets_added\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_required_sheets_exist\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_task_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_data_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoMacros::test_no_vba_macros\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoMacros::test_file_extension_xlsx\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_exports_have_data\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_imports_have_data\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_gdp_have_data - ...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_exports_values - Ass...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_imports_values - Ass...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_gdp_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_have_data\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_values\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_statistics_have_data\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_min_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_max_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_median_values - Asse...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_mean_values - Assert...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_percentile_values - ...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_has_data\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_values_reasonable\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_values\n======================== 17 failed, 10 passed in 3.41s =========================\n\n--- stderr ---\n", "system_prompt_chars": 32071}
{"trial_id": "sb__offer-letter-generator__sz50__hard__s1", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "offer-letter-generator", "pool_size": 50, "noise_mode": "hard", "seed": 1, "gt_slugs": ["docx"], "gt_positions": [5], "n_candidates": 50, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 151.9, "agent_stdout_tail": "The filled offer letter has been saved to `root/offer_letter_filled.docx` (which maps to `/root/offer_letter_filled.docx`). Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n- **All `{{PLACEHOLDER}}`s** replaced with values from `employee_data.json` using paragraph-level rebuilding (handles Word's split-run XML quirk)\n- **Nested tables** traversed recursively to fill `{{POSITION}}`, `{{DEPARTMENT}}`, `{{START_DATE}}`, `{{MANAGER_NAME}}`, `{{BASE_SALARY}}`, `{{SIGNING_BONUS}}`, `{{EQUITY_SHARES}}`\n- **`{{IF_RELOCATION}}...{{END_IF_RELOCATION}}`** \u2014 since `RELOCATION_PACKAGE` is `\"Yes\"`, the relocation paragraph content was kept and both marker tags removed, leaving the clean sentence: *\"You are eligible for a relocation package of $15,000. This includes moving expenses and temporary housing for 30 days.\"*\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": true, "test_log_tail": "test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[DEPARTMENT] PASSED       [ 72%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[BASE_SALARY] PASSED      [ 77%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[SIGNING_BONUS] PASSED    [ 83%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[EQUITY_SHARES] PASSED    [ 88%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[MANAGER_NAME] PASSED     [ 94%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_conditional_section PASSED                  [100%]\n\n==================================== PASSES ====================================\n=========================== short test summary info ============================\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_no_remaining_placeholders\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::test_split_placeholder_replaced[DATE]\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py: