{"trial_id": "sb__weighted-gdp-calc__sz20__hard__s2", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "weighted-gdp-calc", "pool_size": 20, "noise_mode": "hard", "seed": 2, "gt_slugs": ["xlsx"], "gt_positions": [11], "n_candidates": 20, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 724.3, "agent_stdout_tail": "All three steps are complete. The file `/tmp/gdp.xlsx` now has:\n\n**Step 1 \u2014 INDEX/MATCH lookups (H12:L17, H19:L24, H26:L31):**\n- Formula: `=INDEX(Data!$H$21:$M$40,MATCH($D{row},Data!$B$21:$B$40,0),MATCH({col}$9,Data!$H$4:$M$4,0))`\n- Uses two conditions: series code from column D and year from row 9 to pull exports, imports, and GDP for all 6 GCC countries (UAE, Bahrain, Kuwait, Qatar, Oman, Saudi Arabia) across 2019\u20132023.\n\n**Step 2 \u2014 Net Exports as % of GDP (H35:L40) + Statistics:**\n- Net exports formula: `=(exports - imports) / GDP * 100`\n- Statistics rows 42\u201347: MIN, MAX, MEDIAN, AVERAGE, PERCENTILE(0.25), PERCENTILE(0.75)\n\n**Step 3 \u2014 GDP-Weighted Mean (H50:L50):**\n- Formula: `=SUMPRODUCT(H26:H31,H35:H40)/SUM(H26:H31)` \u2014 weights each country's net exports % by its GDP\n- 2019: **12.22%**, 2020: **6.84%**, 2021: **15.58%**, 2022: **22.35%**, 2023: **14.86%**\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "NoExcelErrors::test_no_formula_errors\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_no_extra_sheets_added\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_required_sheets_exist\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_task_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_data_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoMacros::test_no_vba_macros\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoMacros::test_file_extension_xlsx\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_exports_have_data\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_imports_have_data\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormu