{"trial_id": "sb__setup-fuzzing-py__sz5__easy__s0", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "setup-fuzzing-py", "pool_size": 5, "noise_mode": "easy", "seed": 0, "gt_slugs": ["discover-important-function", "fuzzing-python", "setup-env"], "gt_positions": [2, 3, 4], "n_candidates": 5, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 765.4, "agent_stdout_tail": "All 5 steps complete. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n**Step 1** \u2014 `/app/libraries.txt` lists: arrow, black, ipython, minisgl, ujson\n\n**Step 2** \u2014 `notes_for_testing.txt` written for each library analyzing key fuzz targets:\n- **arrow**: `DateTimeParser.parse_iso()` / `ArrowFactory.get()` \u2014 datetime string parsing\n- **black**: `format_str()` / `lib2to3_parse()` \u2014 Python source code formatting with idempotence oracle\n- **ipython**: `TransformerManager.transform_cell()` \u2014 IPython magic/system/help syntax transformations\n- **minisgl**: `deserialize_type()` \u2014 JSON-to-typed-object deserialization\n- **ujson**: `ujson.loads()` \u2014 C-based JSON decoder (memory safety focus)\n\n**Step 3** \u2014 `fuzz.py` written for each library using Atheris with `FuzzedDataProvider` for structured input generation\n\n**Step 4** \u2014 `.venv` created in each library root using `uv venv --system-site-packages` (inheriting system atheris/torch), then installed each library with `uv pip install -e .`\n\n**Step 5** \u2014 Each fuzzer ran 10 seconds, logs saved to `fuzz.log`:\n- arrow: 210,387 runs\n- black: 24,027 runs (found real `KeyError: '~='` bug during testing)\n- ipython: 68,766 runs (found `SystemError` in tokenizer during testing)\n- minisgl: 986,184 runs\n- ujson: 4,849,522 runs (C extension \u2014 fastest)\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "============================= test session starts ==============================\ncollecting ... collected 0 items\n\n============================ no tests ran in 0.00s =============================\n\n--- stderr ---\nERROR: file or directory not found: /tmp/exec_prefill/sb__setup-fuzzing-py__sz5__easy__s0/work/.tests/test_outputs.py\n\n", "system_prompt_chars": 34777}
{"trial_id": "sb__setup-fuzzing-py__sz5__hard__s4", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "setup-fuzzing-py", "pool_size": 5, "noise_mode": "hard", "seed": 4, "gt_slugs": ["discover-important-function", "fuzzing-python", "setup-env"], "gt_positions": [0, 1, 3], "n_candidates": 5, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 866.5, "agent_stdout_tail": "All steps completed successfully:\n\n**Step 1** \u2014 `/app/libraries.txt` lists all 5 libraries: arrow, black, ipython, minisgl, ujson.\n\n**Step 2** \u2014 Analysis notes written to `notes_for_testing.txt` for each library:\n- **arrow**: targets `DateTimeParser.parse_iso()` / `ArrowFactory.get()` for datetime string parsing\n- **black**: targets `format_str()` for Python code formatting\n- **IPython**: targets `TransformerManager.transform_cell()` / `check_complete()` for cell transformation\n- **minisgl**: targets `deserialize_type()` for message deserialization\n- **ujson**: targets `ujson.loads()` for JSON parsing of the C extension\n\n**Step 3** \u2014 LibFuzzer fuzz drivers (`fuzz.py`) created for all 5 libraries using Atheris.\n\n**Step 4** \u2014 Python 3.12 virtual environments set up at `/app/<lib>/.venv` for all 5 libraries, with each library installed in editable mode plus Atheris.\n\n**Step 5** \u2014 All 5 fuzzers ran for 10 seconds and logs saved to `/app/<lib>/fuzz.log`:\n- `arrow`: 64,649 runs \u2014 discovered datetime parsing paths\n- `black`: 29,204 runs \u2014 found a real `KeyError` bug in the parser (fixed in harness)\n- `ipython`: 79,632 runs \u2014 exercised cell transformation logic\n- `ujson`: 3,059,932 runs \u2014 high-speed testing of C JSON parser\n- `minisgl`: 623,187 runs \u2014 tested message deserialization\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "============================= test session starts ==============================\ncollecting ... collected 0 items\n\n============================ no tests ran in 0.00s =============================\n\n--- stderr ---\nERROR: file or directory not found: /tmp/exec_prefill/sb__setup-fuzzing-py__sz5__hard__s4/work/.tests/test_outputs.py\n\n", "system_prompt_chars": 35231}
{"trial_id": "sb__weighted-gdp-calc__sz50__random__s1", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "weighted-gdp-calc", "pool_size": 50, "noise_mode": "random", "seed": 1, "gt_slugs": ["xlsx"], "gt_positions": [33], "n_candidates": 50, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 294.1, "agent_stdout_tail": "All three steps are complete. Here's what was done to `gdp.xlsx`:\n\n**Step 1 \u2014 H12:L17, H19:L24, H26:L31 (yellow cells)**\nFilled with `INDEX/MATCH` formulas using two conditions:\n```\n=INDEX(Data!$H$21:$M$40, MATCH($D12,Data!$B$21:$B$40,0), MATCH(H$9,Data!$H$4:$M$4,0))\n```\n- Row condition: series code from column D matched against `Data!$B$21:$B$40`\n- Column condition: year from row 9 matched against `Data!$H$4:$M$4` (2018\u20132023 headers)\n\n**Step 2 \u2014 Net Exports % of GDP (H35:L40 + stats rows 42\u201347)**\nNet exports formula: `=(H12-H19)/H26*100` (Exports \u2212 Imports) \u00f7 GDP \u00d7 100, correctly wired per country. Computed values range ~0%\u201337% across 2019\u20132023 for the 6 GCC countries. Statistics added: `MIN`, `MAX`, `MEDIAN`, `AVERAGE`, `PERCENTILE(...,0.25)`, `PERCENTILE(...,0.75)`.\n\n**Step 3 \u2014 Weighted Mean (H50:L50)**\n```\n=SUMPRODUCT(H26:H31,H35:H40)/SUM(H26:H31)\n```\nWeights each country's net-exports-%-of-GDP by that country's nominal GDP, yielding the GDP-weighted GCC average (~6.8% in 2020, ~22.4% in 2022).\n\nCell formatting (yellow fills, fonts, colors) was preserved throughout; the Data sheet was not modified.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_exports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_imports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_gdp_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_statistics_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_has_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoExcelErrors::test_no_formula_errors\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_no_extra_sheets_added\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_required_sheets_exist\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_task_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_data_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoMacros::test_no_vba_macros\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoMacros::test_file_extension_xlsx\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_exports_values - Ass...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_imports_values - Ass...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_gdp_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_values\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_min_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_max_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_median_values - Asse...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_mean_values - Assert...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_percentile_values - ...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_values_reasonable\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_values\n======================== 11 failed, 16 passed in 3.54s =========================\n\n--- stderr ---\n", "system_prompt_chars": 42757}
{"trial_id": "sb__setup-fuzzing-py__sz5__easy__s1", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "setup-fuzzing-py", "pool_size": 5, "noise_mode": "easy", "seed": 1, "gt_slugs": ["discover-important-function", "fuzzing-python", "setup-env"], "gt_positions": [0, 1, 3], "n_candidates": 5, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 678.9, "agent_stdout_tail": "All 5 steps are complete. Here's a summary:\n\n**Step 1** \u2014 `/app/libraries.txt` lists all 5 libraries: arrow, black, ipython, minisgl, ujson.\n\n**Step 2** \u2014 `notes_for_testing.txt` written for each library with analysis of key fuzzing targets:\n- **arrow**: `arrow.get()` string date/time parsing\n- **black**: `black.format_str()` Python code formatting\n- **ipython**: `TransformerManager.transform_cell()` IPython input transformation\n- **minisgl**: `deserialize_type()` message deserialization from untrusted dicts\n- **ujson**: `ujson.loads()` C-extension JSON decoder\n\n**Step 3** \u2014 `fuzz.py` Atheris LibFuzzer drivers created for each library using `FuzzedDataProvider` for structured inputs and appropriate exception handling.\n\n**Step 4** \u2014 `.venv` created for each library with `--system-site-packages` (to inherit the pre-installed `atheris`) plus library-specific dependencies installed via pip.\n\n**Step 5** \u2014 All fuzzers ran successfully for ~10 seconds, logs saved to `fuzz.log`:\n- **arrow**: 174,462 runs, 15,860 exec/s, cov: 206\n- **black**: ~54,000 runs, 5,442 exec/s, cov: 1,646\n- **ipython**: ~43,000 runs, 10,904 exec/s, cov: 193\n- **minisgl**: 3,037,884 runs, 276,171 exec/s (torch excluded from instrumentation)\n- **ujson**: 5,550,039 runs, 504,549 exec/s (C extension, no Python instrumentation)\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "============================= test session starts ==============================\ncollecting ... collected 0 items\n\n============================ no tests ran in 0.00s =============================\n\n--- stderr ---\nERR