{"trial_id": "sb__offer-letter-generator__sz100__random__s1", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "offer-letter-generator", "pool_size": 100, "noise_mode": "random", "seed": 1, "gt_slugs": ["docx"], "gt_positions": [82], "n_candidates": 100, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 152.7, "agent_stdout_tail": "The offer letter has been generated and saved to `/root/offer_letter_filled.docx`. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n**Data used** (`employee_data.json`):\n- Candidate: **Sarah Chen** \u2014 Senior Software Engineer, Platform Engineering\n- Company: **Nexus Technologies Inc.**, Start date: February 12, 2024\n- Salary: $185,000 + $25,000 signing bonus + 5,000 equity shares\n- Manager: Michael Rodriguez | HR: Jennifer Walsh\n\n**Key handling**:\n- **Split placeholders** \u2014 Many tokens were fragmented across Word XML runs (e.g., `{{COMP` + `ANY_NAME}}`). The script reconstructed each paragraph's full text before replacing, then rebuilt the runs cleanly.\n- **Conditional relocation section** \u2014 Since `RELOCATION_PACKAGE = \"Yes\"`, the content between `{{IF_RELOCATION}}` and `{{END_IF_RELOCATION}}` was **kept** and the markers were removed, resulting in: *\"You are eligible for a relocation package of $15,000. This includes moving expenses and temporary housing for 30 days.\"*\n- **Headers/footers** \u2014 `{{DOC_ID}}` \u2192 `OFFER-2024-00847` and `{{COMPANY_NAME}}` in the footer were also filled correctly.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": true, "test_log_tail": "test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[DEPARTMENT] PASSED       [ 72%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[BASE_SALARY] PASSED      [ 77%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[SIGNING_BONUS] PASSED    [ 83%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[EQUITY_SHARES] PASSED    [ 88%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[MANAGER_NAME] PASSED     [ 94%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_conditional_section PASSED                  [100%]\n\n