{"trial_id": "sb__weighted-gdp-calc__sz50__hard__s1", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "weighted-gdp-calc", "pool_size": 50, "noise_mode": "hard", "seed": 1, "gt_slugs": ["xlsx"], "gt_positions": [20], "n_candidates": 50, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 281.6, "agent_stdout_tail": "All done. Here's a summary of what was implemented in `gdp.xlsx`:\n\n**Step 1 \u2014 INDEX/MATCH lookups (H12:L17, H19:L24, H26:L31)**\nEach yellow cell uses `INDEX/MATCH` with two conditions:\n- Row lookup: `MATCH($D{row}, Data!$B$21:$B$40, 0)` \u2014 matches the series code in column D against Data column B\n- Column lookup: `MATCH({col}$9, Data!$H$4:$M$4, 0)` \u2014 matches the year in row 9 against Data row 4 headers\n\nExample for H12 (UAE exports 2019):\n```\n=INDEX(Data!$H$21:$M$40,MATCH($D12,Data!$B$21:$B$40,0),MATCH(H$9,Data!$H$4:$M$4,0))\n```\n\n**Step 2 \u2014 Net Exports % GDP (H35:L40)**\n`=(Exports \u2212 Imports) / GDP \u00d7 100` \u2014 e.g. UAE: `=(H12\u2212H19)/H26*100`\n\n**Statistics (H42:L47):** MIN, MAX, MEDIAN, AVERAGE, PERCENTILE at 0.25 and 0.75 over the 6-country range.\n\n**Step 3 \u2014 GDP-weighted mean (H50:L50)**\n```\n=SUMPRODUCT(H26:H31, H35:H40) / SUM(H26:H31)\n```\nThis weights each country's net export % by its GDP share. The 2019 weighted mean is **~12.2%**, rising to **~22.4%** in 2022 when oil prices were elevated.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_exports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_imports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_gdp_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_statistics_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_has_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoExcelErrors::test_no_formula_errors\nPASSED .tests/test_outp