{"trial_id": "sb__setup-fuzzing-py__sz5__easy__s4", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "setup-fuzzing-py", "pool_size": 5, "noise_mode": "easy", "seed": 4, "gt_slugs": ["discover-important-function", "fuzzing-python", "setup-env"], "gt_positions": [0, 2, 4], "n_candidates": 5, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 783.1, "agent_stdout_tail": "All 5 steps are complete:\n\n**Step 1** \u2014 `libraries.txt` lists: `arrow`, `ujson`, `black`, `ipython`, `minisgl`\n\n**Step 2** \u2014 `notes_for_testing.txt` written for each library, documenting key fuzz targets:\n- **arrow**: `arrow.get()` / `DateTimeParser.parse()` for datetime string parsing\n- **ujson**: `ujson.loads()` / `ujson.dumps()` \u2014 C extension JSON codec\n- **black**: `black.format_str()` \u2014 Python source code formatter\n- **ipython**: `TransformerManager.transform_cell()` \u2014 IPython cell input transformer\n- **minisgl**: `_PARSE_MEM_BYTES()` + math utils (`div_ceil`, `div_even`, etc.) \u2014 pure-Python components avoiding heavy ML deps\n\n**Step 3** \u2014 `fuzz.py` written for each library using Atheris/LibFuzzer with `atheris.instrument_all()` for coverage and proper exception filtering\n\n**Step 4** \u2014 `.venv` created using Python 3.12 (system Python) for each library with library deps installed and atheris symlinked in from the user install\n\n**Step 5** \u2014 All fuzzers ran for 10 seconds; `fuzz.log` saved for each. Summary:\n- `arrow`: 124K runs, 38 Instrumenting lines, INITED + 42 NEW/pulse events\n- `ujson`: 5.9M runs (fast C extension), 3 Instrumenting lines, INITED + pulse events  \n- `black`: 35K runs, 156 Instrumenting lines, INITED + 266 NEW/pulse events\n- `ipython`: 70K runs, 557 Instrumenting lines, INITED + 207 NEW/pulse events\n- `minisgl`: 2.7M runs, Instrumenting 3095 functions, INITED + 7 NEW/pulse events\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "============================= test session starts ==============================\ncollecting ... collected 0 items\n\n============================ no tests ran in 0.00s =============================\n\n--- stderr ---\nERROR: file or directory not found: /tmp/exec_prefill/sb__setup-fuzzing-py__sz5__easy__s4/work/.tests/test_outputs.py\n\n", "system_prompt_chars": 34777}
{"trial_id": "sb__weighted-gdp-calc__sz50__hard__s2", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "weighted-gdp-calc", "pool_size": 50, "noise_mode": "hard", "seed": 2, "gt_slugs": ["xlsx"], "gt_positions": [28], "n_candidates": 50, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 368.7, "agent_stdout_tail": "All done. Here's a summary of what was done to `gdp.xlsx`:\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 INDEX&MATCH lookups (H12:L17, H19:L24, H26:L31)**\n\nEach yellow cell uses:\n```\n=INDEX(Data!$H$21:$M$40, MATCH($D<row>, Data!$B$21:$B$40, 0), MATCH(<col>$9, Data!$H$4:$M$4, 0))\n```\n- First `MATCH` finds the row by **series code** (column D in Task \u2192 column B in Data)\n- Second `MATCH` finds the column by **year** (row 9 in Task \u2192 row 4 in Data)\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Net exports % of GDP (H35:L40) + Statistics**\n\n- Net exports formula: `=(Exports - Imports) / GDP \u00d7 100` for each country/year pair\n- Min, Max, Median, Average, 25th/75th percentiles calculated over the 6-country column range\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 GDP-weighted mean (H50:L50)**\n\n```\n=SUMPRODUCT(H26:H31, H35:H40) / SUM(H26:H31)\n```\nThis weights each country's net exports % by its GDP share. Sample results:\n| Year | Weighted Mean (% GDP) |\n|------|----------------------|\n| 2019 | 12.22% |\n| 2020 | 6.84% |\n| 2021 | 15.58% |\n| 2022 | 22.35% |\n| 2023 | 14.86% |\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "NoExcelErrors::test_no_formula_errors\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_no_extra_sheets_added\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_required_sheets_exist\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_task_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_data_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoMacros::test_no_vba_macros\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoMacros::test_file_extension_xlsx\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_exports_have_data\nFAILED 