{"trial_id": "sb__weighted-gdp-calc__sz50__hard__s4", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "weighted-gdp-calc", "pool_size": 50, "noise_mode": "hard", "seed": 4, "gt_slugs": ["xlsx"], "gt_positions": [35], "n_candidates": 50, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 239.3, "agent_stdout_tail": "All formulas are correctly in place and the yellow cell formatting is preserved. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n**Step 1 \u2014 `H12:L17`, `H19:L24`, `H26:L31`** (Exports, Imports, GDP lookup):\n```\n=INDEX(Data!$H$21:$M$40, MATCH($D12, Data!$B$21:$B$40, 0), MATCH(H$9, Data!$H$4:$M$4, 0))\n```\n- First MATCH finds the row by series code (column D, locked) in Data column B (rows 21\u201340)\n- Second MATCH finds the column by year (row 9, locked) in Data row 4 headers (2018\u20132023)\n- The `$` anchoring ensures the formula copies correctly across all 5 years and 6 countries\n\n**Step 2a \u2014 `H35:L40`** (Net Exports % of GDP):\n```\n=(H12-H19)/H26*100   \u2190 UAE row example\n```\nEach row subtracts Imports from Exports and divides by GDP \u00d7 100, referencing the already-filled data above.\n\n**Step 2b \u2014 `H42:L47`** (Statistics across 6 GCC countries per year):\n- Row 42: `=MIN(H35:H40)`\n- Row 43: `=MAX(H35:H40)`\n- Row 44: `=MEDIAN(H35:H40)`\n- Row 45: `=AVERAGE(H35:H40)`\n- Row 46: `=PERCENTILE(H35:H40,0.25)`\n- Row 47: `=PERCENTILE(H35:H40,0.75)`\n\n**Step 3 \u2014 `H50:L50`** (GDP-weighted mean):\n```\n=SUMPRODUCT(H35:H40, H26:H31) / SUM(H26:H31)\n```\nThis weights each country's net export % by its nominal GDP, giving the GCC aggregate net exports as a share of total GCC GDP.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_exports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_imports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_gdp_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_have_data\nPASSED 