{"trial_id": "sb__weighted-gdp-calc__sz50__easy__s0", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "weighted-gdp-calc", "pool_size": 50, "noise_mode": "easy", "seed": 0, "gt_slugs": ["xlsx"], "gt_positions": [29], "n_candidates": 50, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 224.5, "agent_stdout_tail": "All formula cells are correctly filled. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n**Step 1 \u2014 `H12:L17`, `H19:L24`, `H26:L31`:** Filled with `INDEX/MATCH` formulas using two conditions \u2014 series code (column D) and year (row 9):\n```\n=INDEX(Data!$H$21:$M$40, MATCH($D12, Data!$B$21:$B$40, 0), MATCH(H$9, Data!$H$4:$M$4, 0))\n```\n\n**Step 2 \u2014 `H35:L40`:** Net exports as % of GDP for each GCC country:\n```\n=(exports \u2212 imports) / GDP \u00d7 100\n```\nStatistics (min, max, median, mean, 25th/75th percentiles) filled in `H42:L47`.\n\n**Step 3 \u2014 `H50:L50`:** GDP-weighted mean using SUMPRODUCT:\n```\n=SUMPRODUCT(H26:H31, H35:H40) / SUM(H26:H31)\n```\n\n**Computed weighted mean results:** ~12.2% (2019), ~6.8% (2020), ~15.6% (2021), ~22.4% (2022), ~14.9% (2023) \u2014 reflecting GCC's export-heavy economies, with the 2020 dip driven by the oil price crash and COVID.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_exports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_imports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_gdp_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_statistics_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_has_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoExcelErrors::test_no_formula_errors\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_no_extra_sheets_added\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_required_sheets_exist\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormatting