{"trial_id": "sb__offer-letter-generator__sz100__hard__s2", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "offer-letter-generator", "pool_size": 100, "noise_mode": "hard", "seed": 2, "gt_slugs": ["docx"], "gt_positions": [2], "n_candidates": 100, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 168.0, "agent_stdout_tail": "The offer letter has been filled successfully. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n**Template:** `offer_letter_template.docx` \u2192 **Output:** `root/offer_letter_filled.docx`\n\n**Key challenges handled:**\n- **Split placeholders** \u2014 Word splits text like `{{COMP` + `ANY_NAME}}` across multiple XML runs. The script collects the full paragraph text, replaces placeholders at the paragraph level, then writes the result into the first run and clears the rest.\n- **Nested tables** \u2014 The Employment Details table contains nested sub-tables (Basic Information + Compensation). The `process_table()` function recurses into `cell.tables` to find and fill those.\n- **Conditional section** \u2014 `RELOCATION_PACKAGE` is `\"Yes\"`, so the `{{IF_RELOCATION}}...{{END_IF_RELOCATION}}` markers are stripped while the content (relocation package of $15,000, 30 days housing) is retained and its inner placeholders (`{{RELOCATION_AMOUNT}}`, `{{RELOCATION_DAYS}}`) are filled.\n- **Headers & Footers** \u2014 `Document ID: OFFER-2024-00847` in the header and the confidential footer are both filled correctly.\n\n**All 20+ placeholders replaced, 0 remaining.**\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": true, "test_log_tail": "test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[DEPARTMENT] PASSED       [ 72%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[BASE_SALARY] PASSED      [ 77%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[SIGNING_BONUS] PASSED    [ 83%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[EQUITY_SHARES] PASSED    [ 88%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_nested_table_value[MANAGER_NAME] PASSED     [ 94%]\n.tests/test_outputs.py::test_conditional_section PASSED   