{"trial_id": "sb__weighted-gdp-calc__sz50__easy__s2", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "weighted-gdp-calc", "pool_size": 50, "noise_mode": "easy", "seed": 2, "gt_slugs": ["xlsx"], "gt_positions": [38], "n_candidates": 50, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 350.1, "agent_stdout_tail": "All 155 formulas have been successfully written to `gdp.xlsx`. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n**Step 1 \u2014 H12:L17, H19:L24, H26:L31** (90 cells): Filled with `INDEX&MATCH` formulas using two conditions \u2014 series code from column D and year from row 9:\n```\n=INDEX(Data!$H$21:$M$40, MATCH($D12,Data!$B$21:$B$40,0), MATCH(H$9,Data!$H$4:$M$4,0))\n```\nThe outer MATCH finds the row by series code in `Data!B21:B40`; the inner MATCH finds the column by year in `Data!H4:M4`.\n\n**Step 2a \u2014 H35:L40** (30 cells): Net exports as % of GDP = (Exports \u2212 Imports) / GDP \u00d7 100:\n```\n=(H12-H19)/H26*100\n```\nExpected values (2019\u20132023): UAE ~20\u201325%, Bahrain ~11\u201326%, Kuwait ~13\u201330%, Qatar ~14\u201337%, Oman ~2\u201320%, Saudi Arabia ~0\u201317%.\n\n**Step 2b \u2014 H42:L47** (30 cells): MIN, MAX, MEDIAN, AVERAGE, PERCENTILE(0.25), PERCENTILE(0.75) over H35:H40 for each year.\n\n**Step 3 \u2014 H50:L50** (5 cells): GDP-weighted mean using SUMPRODUCT:\n```\n=SUMPRODUCT(H26:H31, H35:H40) / SUM(H26:H31)\n```\nResults: 2019 \u2248 12.2%, 2020 \u2248 6.8%, 2021 \u2248 15.6%, 2022 \u2248 22.4%, 2023 \u2248 14.9%.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_exports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_imports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_gdp_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_statistics_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_has_data\nPASSED .tes