{"trial_id": "sb__weighted-gdp-calc__sz50__easy__s3", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "weighted-gdp-calc", "pool_size": 50, "noise_mode": "easy", "seed": 3, "gt_slugs": ["xlsx"], "gt_positions": [5], "n_candidates": 50, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 294.6, "agent_stdout_tail": "All formulas have been written successfully to `gdp.xlsx`. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n**Step 1 \u2014 INDEX/MATCH lookups (H12:L17, H19:L24, H26:L31):**\nUsed `=INDEX(Data!$H$21:$M$40, MATCH($D{row},Data!$B$21:$B$40,0), MATCH({col}$9,Data!$H$4:$M$4,0))` \u2014 a two-condition lookup that matches the series code (column D) against Data column B, and the year (row 9) against Data row 4 (2018\u20132023 headers). This pulls exports, imports, and GDP for all 6 GCC countries across 5 years (2019\u20132023).\n\n**Step 2 \u2014 Net Exports % of GDP (H35:L40) + Statistics (H42:L47):**\n- Net exports formula: `=(H12\u2212H19)/H26*100` (Exports \u2212 Imports) \u00f7 GDP \u00d7 100, applied per country/year\n- Statistics: `MIN`, `MAX`, `MEDIAN`, `AVERAGE`, `PERCENTILE(...,0.25)`, `PERCENTILE(...,0.75)` over H35:H40 for each year column\n\n**Step 3 \u2014 GDP-weighted mean (H50:L50):**\n`=SUMPRODUCT(H26:H31, H35:H40)/SUM(H26:H31)` \u2014 weights each country's net export % by its nominal GDP. Sample results: 2019 \u2248 12.2%, 2020 \u2248 6.8%, 2021 \u2248 15.6%, 2022 \u2248 22.4%, 2023 \u2248 14.9%.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_exports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_imports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_gdp_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_statistics_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_has_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoExcelErrors::test_no_formula_errors\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_no_extra_sheets_added\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_required_sheets_exist\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_task_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_data_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoMacros::test_no_vba_macros\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoMacros::test_file_extension_xlsx\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_exports_values - Ass...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_imports_values - Ass...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_gdp_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_values\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_min_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_max_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_median_values - Asse...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_mean_values - Assert...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_percentile_values - ...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_values_reasonable\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_values\n======================== 11 failed, 16 passed in 3.80s =========================\n\n--- stderr ---\n", "system_prompt_chars": 40195}
{"trial_id": "sb__weighted-gdp-calc__sz50__easy__s4", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "weighted-gdp-calc", "pool_size": 50, "noise_mode": "easy", "seed": 4, "gt_slugs": ["xlsx"], "gt_positions": [47], "n_candidates": 50, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 248.1, "agent_stdout_tail": "All formulas are correctly in place. Here's a summary of everything done to `gdp.xlsx`:\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2014 H12:L17, H19:L24, H26:L31** (Exports, Imports, GDP lookups)\n\nUsed `INDEX`+`MATCH` with two conditions \u2014 series code from column D and year from row 9:\n```\n=INDEX(Data!$H$21:$M$40, MATCH($D12, Data!$B$21:$B$40, 0), MATCH(H$9, Data!$H$4:$M$4, 0))\n```\n- Row MATCH: looks up the series code (e.g. `466BXGS_BP6.A`) in `Data!$B$21:$B$40`\n- Column MATCH: looks up the year (e.g. 2019) in `Data!$H$4:$M$4`\n- Dollar signs ensure correct anchoring when copying across rows and columns\n\n---\n\n**Step 2a \u2014 H35:L40** (Net Exports % of GDP)\n\n```\n=(H12-H19)/H26*100\n```\nEach row subtracts that country's imports from exports, divides by GDP, multiplies by 100.\n\n**Step 2b \u2014 H42:L47** (Statistics per year column)\n\n| Row | Formula |\n|-----|---------|\n| 42 | `=MIN(H35:H40)` |\n| 43 | `=MAX(H35:H40)` |\n| 44 | `=MEDIAN(H35:H40)` |\n| 45 | `=AVERAGE(H35:H40)` |\n| 46 | `=PERCENTILE(H35:H40,0.25)` |\n| 47 | `=PERCENTILE(H35:H40,0.75)` |\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2014 H50:L50** (GDP-weighted mean)\n\n```\n=SUMPRODUCT(H35:H40, H26:H31) / SUM(H26:H31)\n```\nWeights each country's net-export % by its nominal GDP, yielding the GCC aggregate weighted mean (~12.2% in 2019, rising to ~22.4% in 2022). All original cell formatting (yellow fills, colors, fonts) was preserved.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_exports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_imports_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1LookupFormulas::test_gdp_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_statistics_have_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_has_data\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoExcelErrors::test_no_formula_errors\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_no_extra_sheets_added\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_required_sheets_exist\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_task_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_data_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoMacros::test_no_vba_macros\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestNoMacros::test_file_extension_xlsx\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_exports_values - Ass...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_imports_values - Ass...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep1DataValues::test_gdp_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2NetExportsCalculation::test_net_exports_pct_values\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_min_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_max_values - Asserti...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_median_values - Asse...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_mean_values - Assert...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep2Statistics::test_percentile_values - ...\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_values_reasonable\nFAILED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestStep3WeightedMean::test_weighted_mean_values\n======================== 11 failed, 16 passed in 3.59s =========================\n\n--- stderr ---\n", "system_prompt_chars": 40195}
{"trial_id": "sb__setup-fuzzing-py__sz10__hard__s2", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "setup-fuzzing-py", "pool_size": 10, "noise_mode": "hard", "seed": 2, "gt_slugs": ["discover-important-function", "fuzzing-python", "setup-env"], "gt_positions": [3, 5, 7], "n_candidates": 10, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 708.3, "agent_stdout_tail": "All 5 steps completed successfully. Here's a summary:\n\n**Step 1 \u2014 `libraries.txt`**: Listed all 5 library paths: `arrow`, `black`, `ipython`, `minisgl`, `ujson`.\n\n**Step 2 \u2014 `notes_for_testing.txt`** (per library):\n- **arrow**: Targets `arrow.get(string)` / `arrow.get(string, fmt)` \u2014 datetime string parsing\n- **black**: Targets `black.format_str(src, mode)` \u2014 Python code formatting pipeline  \n- **ipython**: Targets `TransformerManager.transform_cell(cell)` \u2014 IPython input transformation\n- **minisgl**: Targets `SamplingParams` construction + `is_greedy` property \u2014 ML parameter validation\n- **ujson**: Targets `ujson.loads(data)` \u2014 JSON parsing via C extension\n\n**Step 3 \u2014 `fuzz.py`**: Atheris/LibFuzzer drivers created for each library using `FuzzedDataProvider` for structured input generation.\n\n**Step 4 \u2014 `.venv`**: Python 3.12 virtual environments with `--system-site-packages` (to access pre-installed `atheris`) created for each library.\n\n**Step 5 \u2014 `fuzz.log`**: All 5 fuzzers completed 10-second runs:\n| Library | Runs | Notable |\n|---------|------|---------|\n| arrow | 239,405 | Clean run |\n| black | 53,176 | Found real bug: `KeyError: '~='` in blib2to3's opmap |\n| ipython | 74,516 | Found real bug: `SystemError` in Python's C tokenizer |\n| minisgl | 1,104,863 | Clean run |\n| ujson | 3,076,122 | C extension (coverage-blind but crash-detects) |\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "============================= test session starts ==============================\ncollecting ... collected 0 items\n\n============================ no tests ran in 0.00s =============================\n\n--- stderr ---\nERROR: file or directory not found: /tmp/exec_prefill/sb__setup-fuzzing-py__sz10__hard__s2/work/.tests/test_outputs.py\n\n", "system_prompt_chars": 39407}
