{"trial_id": "sb__weighted-gdp-calc__sz100__random__s4", "dataset": "sb", "task_id": "weighted-gdp-calc", "pool_size": 100, "noise_mode": "random", "seed": 4, "gt_slugs": ["xlsx"], "gt_positions": [97], "n_candidates": 100, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "agent_rc": 0, "agent_wall_s": 285.9, "agent_stdout_tail": "All formulas are correctly in place in `gdp.xlsx`. Here's a summary of what's complete:\n\n**Step 1 \u2014 INDEX/MATCH lookups (H12:L17, H19:L24, H26:L31):**\nAll 90 cells filled with `=INDEX(Data!$H$21:$M$40, MATCH($D{row},Data!$B$21:$B$40,0), MATCH({col}$9,Data!$H$4:$M$4,0))` \u2014 matching on series code (column D) and year (row 9, 2019\u20132023).\n\n**Step 2 \u2014 Net Exports % of GDP (H35:L40):**\n`=(Exports - Imports)/GDP * 100` for each of the 6 GCC countries. Computed values:\n\n| Country | 2019 | 2020 | 2021 | 2022 | 2023 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| UAE | 19.7% | 21.9% | 25.2% | 24.8% | 23.2% |\n| Bahrain | 11.3% | 5.6% | 19.5% | 25.9% | 17.3% |\n| Kuwait | 12.6% | 5.6% | 22.4% | 30.1% | 20.9% |\n| Qatar | 14.3% | 8.2% | 24.7% | 36.9% | 27.5% |\n| Oman | 12.5% | 2.5% | 10.6% | 20.4% | 14.8% |\n| Saudi Arabia | 8.0% | 0.1% | 8.3% | 16.9% | 7.2% |\n\nStats rows (42\u201347): MIN, MAX, MEDIAN, AVERAGE, PERCENTILE(25%), PERCENTILE(75%) all present.\n\n**Step 3 \u2014 GDP-weighted mean (H50:L50):**\n`=SUMPRODUCT(GDP_range, NX%_range)/SUM(GDP_range)` \u2014 results:\n- 2019: **~12.2%**\n- 2020: **~6.8%**\n- 2021: **~15.6%**\n- 2022: **~22.4%**\n- 2023: **~14.9%**\n\nThe file `~/gdp.xlsx` is complete with all required formulas intact and no formatting changes made.\n", "agent_stderr_tail": "", "pass": false, "test_log_tail": "NoExcelErrors::test_no_formula_errors\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_no_extra_sheets_added\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestSheetStructure::test_required_sheets_exist\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormattingPreserved::test_task_sheet_column_widths\nPASSED .tests/test_outputs.py::TestFormatting